C o m p i l a t i o n


      Reservoir Problem
      September 15, 2015
   5   
   6  * 1. DEFINE the SETS
   7  SETS time  month /1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6/
   8       spatial water flow /turbine,irrigation,reservoir,spill,A/;
   9   
  10   
  11  * 2. DEFINE input data
  12  PARAMETERS
  13   
  14   
  15     inflow(time) Inflow
  16           /1 2,
  17            2 2,
  18            3 3,
  19            4 4,
  20            5 3,
  21            6 2/;
  22   
  23  SCALARS
  24      reservoirmax     reservoir capcaity          /9/
  25      reservoirinit    reservoir initial storage  /5/
  26      turbinemax    Turbine capacity             /4/
  27      Amin     Minimum flow at A                /1/ ;
  28   
  29  TABLE A(time,spatial) Benifits
  30             turbine  irrigation  reservoir   spill   A
  31   1         1.6      1.0         0           0       0
  32   2         1.7      1.2         0           0       0
  33   3         1.8      1.9         0           0       0
  34   4         1.9      2.0         0           0       0
  35   5         2.0      2.2         0           0       0
  36   6         2.0      2.2         0           0       0;
  37   
  38  * 3. DEFINE the variables
  39  VARIABLES
  40      X(time,spatial) Quantity of water flow each month to each location,
  41      VCOST  total benifits ($);
  42   
  43   
  44   
  45  * Non-negativity constraints
  46  POSITIVE VARIABLES X(time,spatial);
  47   
  48  * 4. COMBINE variables and data in equations
  49  EQUATIONS
  50      COST Total cost ($) and objective function value
  51      resemassbalance(time)     Reservoir storage mass balance
  52      spill(time)       water flow to spill
  53      Aminimum(time)    minimum flow to A
  54      resendstorage           Ending storage >= beginning storage
  55      turbinecap(time)     turbine capacity
  56      resmax(time)      reservoir capacity limit ;
  57   
  58  COST..                 VCOST =E= SUM((time,spatial), A(time,spatial)*X(time,spatial));
  59  resemassbalance(time)..   X(time,'reservoir') - reservoirinit$(ord(time) eq 1)
  60                            - X(time-1,'reservoir')$(ord(time) gt 1)
  61                            =E= inflow(time) - X(time,'turbine') - X(time,'spill');
  62  spill(time)..             X(time,'turbine') + X(time,'spill')
  63                            =E= X(time,'irrigation') + X(time,'A');
  64   
  65  Aminimum(time)..          X(time,'A') =G= Amin;
  66   
  67  resendstorage..           X('6','reservoir') =G= reservoirinit;
  68   
  69  turbinecap(time)..        X(time,'turbine') =L= turbinemax;
  70   
  71  resmax(time)..            X(time,'reservoir') =L= reservoirmax;
  72   
  73  *X.LO('1','irrigation') =  1;
  74  *X.LO('2','irrigation') =  1;
  75  *X.LO('3','irrigation') = 2;
  76   
  77  * 5. DEFINE the MODEL from the EQUATIONS
  78  MODEL Reservoir /ALL/;
  79  *Altnerative way to write (include all previously defined equations)
  80  *MODEL PLANTING /ALL/;
  81   
  82  OPTION LIMROW = 10;
  83  * 6. SOLVE the MODEL
  84  * Solve the Network model using a Linear Programming Solver (see File=>Options=>Solvers)
  85  *     to minimize VCOST
  86  Reservoir.optfile = 1;
  87  SOLVE Reservoir USING LP MAXIMIZING VCOST;
  88   
  89   
  90  * 6. CLick File menu => RUN (F9) or Solve icon and examine solution report in .LST file


